{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3222","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3222","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3222\",\"parent_revision\":\"14cbeb34cab3a426a0190fa6094a73f342658234e4d414b6a25b63dfbdbbf75e\",\"root_revision\":\"14cbeb34cab3a426a0190fa6094a73f342658234e4d414b6a25b63dfbdbbf75e\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-24\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nNo relationship exists anywhere in the backlog schema between a work item and the PR that delivers it. Verified by direct read across the neutral schema and both existing relationship mechanisms.\\n\\nTwo relationship mechanisms already exist and neither models this:\\n\\n- `--parent <epic-id>` (Beads) / sub-issue linking (`create_task_issue`, GitHub) \u2014 item-to-item hierarchy, e.g. an epic and its SAM tasks. Backend-native on both sides, about ownership/decomposition, not \\\"which PR delivers this item.\\\"\\n- `followup_to` (`link_followup`, `operations.py:1839`) \u2014 a genuinely neutral metadata field, deliberately backend-agnostic, using a `P{N}` / `P{N}/T{N}` plan/task address form. But it points at a plan or task, never a PR, and per `docs/backend-providers.md` a PR is neither a work item nor a plan/task \u2014 it has no place in the neutral schema at all today.\\n\\nThe consequence surfaced concretely on #3220: `resolve_item()` (`operations.py:3180`) calls `check_open_prs_for_issue()` (`gh_client.py:1360`), which is GitHub-only (`is:pr is:open #{N}` GraphQL search). On Beads, SQLite, and Memory backends this function is never reachable, so **there is no open-work guard at resolve time on any backend but GitHub** \u2014 a Beads item can be resolved while a PR (or, more generally, any outstanding delivery unit) still depends on it, with no warning at all.\\n\\n#3220 works around the GitHub-only case with an explicit `--pr <N>` argument to `resolve_item`, which lets the caller name and exclude the delivering PR from the guard's search results. That is a one-shot exclusion parameter to a live GitHub search, not a stored relationship, and it does nothing for non-GitHub backends. This item is the follow-up: model the relationship itself, following the `followup_to` precedent (a neutral field, not a GitHub-only live query), so:\\n\\n- The relationship survives independent of a live GitHub search \u2014 set once when the delivering PR is known (e.g. when `/dh:complete-implementation` pushes it), read back without an API round-trip.\\n- Beads and every other backend gets a real open-work guard at resolve time, not silence.\\n- A future non-GitHub \\\"delivery unit\\\" concept (a Beads-native change reference, a GitLab MR) has somewhere to attach without inventing a second mechanism.\\n\\nUser-provided context, from the 2026-08-24 grilling session: the repo owner asked whether the backlog system's existing order/dependency handling (recalling recent work on a Beads `parent` field) already covers this before endorsing the narrower `--pr` fix for #3220. Direct read confirmed `--parent` and `followup_to` are both real but neither models a PR-delivers-item relationship, so this item was filed to carry that gap forward rather than silently drop it once #3220's narrower fix shipped.\\n\\nPoints needing design decisions during grooming, not pre-decided here: the field's name and shape (a single `delivered_by` reference vs a list, since #3219's design allows multiple PRs against one issue); whether it is populated automatically by `/dh:complete-implementation` or requires an explicit call; and whether the GitHub-only guard in `check_open_prs_for_issue` is replaced outright or kept as a supplementary check alongside the new neutral field.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: 2026-08-24 grilling session on #3219/#3220, scoped out of both\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"339af6657e60e05069b6c6e147d7893864589fad6e1b65803c621562f482825b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQg4Z4Q\"}"}